          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "पळवाट (paḷvāṭ) is a Marathi compound built from the stem of पळणे, \"to run away\", inherited from Sanskrit palāyate, \"flees\" (CDIAL 7955), and वाट, \"path\", inherited from Sanskrit vartman, \"track of a wheel, path\" (CDIAL 11366): a path to run by."
            }
